# flux-db Rust patterns

Formatting, naming, docs and lints: see `style.mdc` (Cleanie Flux). Crate layout and design rules: see `architecture.mdc` (Stormie Flux). This file covers implementation patterns only.

## Builders and AST
- Builders are by-value (`fn filter(mut self, ..) -> Self`) and produce owned AST nodes; no lifetimes leaking into public builder types.
- Accept `impl Into<Value>` / `impl Into<Expr>` at API edges; convert once, store concrete types.
- Typed columns are zero-sized or `Copy` handles; `col("x")` builds the same `Column` node.
- Validate identifiers at construction time and return `Result`; never defer validation to rendering.

## Traits and generics
- Drivers are generic parameters (`Executor<D: Driver>`); use native `async fn` in traits (MSRV 1.99, edition 2024), no `async-trait`, no `dyn Driver`.
- Add `Send` bounds where futures cross tasks; return `impl Future + Send` from trait methods when needed.
- Keep traits small; prefer extension traits over growing a core trait.

## Errors
- One `#[non_exhaustive]` `Error` enum in `flux-db-core` (`InvalidQuery`, `Decode`, `NotFound`, `Driver(Box<dyn Error + Send + Sync>)`); no `ErrorKind`, driver errors pass through in `Driver` and are inspected by downcasting. Manual `Display`/`Error` impls, no `anyhow` in library crates.
- No `unwrap`/`expect`/`panic!` in library code except for proven invariants with a comment explaining why.
- Use checked conversions (`TryFrom`) for numeric widths; overflow is an error.

## Performance
- Render SQL into a single pre-sized `String` and a `Vec<Value>`; avoid intermediate `format!` allocations.
- Prefer `&str`/`Cow<'static, str>` for static identifiers; clone only at ownership boundaries.
- Stream large result sets instead of collecting.

## Modules
- One concept per module; `mod.rs`-free layout (`foo.rs` + `foo/`).
- Re-export the public surface from `lib.rs`; keep internals `pub(crate)`.

## Workflow
- Dever Flux may commit and push only to `feature/*` branches, never to `main`, `test` or `dev`. Keep commits small and list the touched files in the flux-db group.
- Gittie Flux opens every PR; Filipe approves and merges.
